  "rationale": "The behavior is mostly there and tested, but the code that produces the file-and-line-range diagnostic has no `{impl}` marker for this requirement. That is a marking gap, and I found no FIXME acknowledging it.\n\n**What works**\n- `validate_evidence_file` (src/evidence.rs ~l.422) reports requirement or example text changes as `\"{label}: {text_field} text changed at {source}\"` followed by `compact_diff`. `{label}` is the evidence file path, which contains the requirement name.\n- `compact_diff` (~l.796) produces the line-oriented diff with `-` for recorded lines and `+` for current lines. It trims the common prefix and suffix and caps output at 8 lines per side.\n- `validate_input_lines` (~l.787) emits `\"input text changed at {file}:{start}-{end}\"` plus `compact_diff`. This is the message that names the file and line range, as the requirement asks.\n- The test `collects_missing_orphan_format_false_and_changed_line_errors` checks the requirement-text error, `- Old text.` and `+ First.`. It also checks the input-text-changed error, `- changed line` and `+ // first line`. Another test (~l.1763) asserts `input text changed at src/main.rs:1-3`, which covers the file and line-range naming. The tests at ~l.1782 and in src/index.rs cover similar diagnostics.\n\n**Gaps**\n1. `validate_input_lines` is marked only with `requirements.ci.inputs`, `requirements.ci.input_containment` and `requirements.configuration.evidence_paths`. It has no `{impl}` for `requirements.ci.diagnostics`. The `references` tool confirms the `{impl}` sites for this requirement are only `inspect_repository`, `inspect_repository_with_progress`, `book_source_dir`, `validate_evidence_file`, `compact_diff` and `display_path`. The input-text diagnostic is a core obligation of this requirement.\n2. `validate_resolved_input` also emits diffs for Rust-item, definition and requirements-glob inputs. It carries no `{impl}` for this requirement either. Those inputs are not literally \"files\", so this is a lesser concern. It still leaves diff behavior that no definition covers.\n3. The `{impl}` markers on `inspect_repository`, `book_source_dir` and `display_path` are broad. They cover other validation messages, such as book.toml errors, that this requirement does not specify.\n4. The message format differs slightly from the requirement's example: the code writes `text changed at md/requirements.md:3` where the example writes `text changed (md/requirements.md:43)`. This is minor, but the output is not exactly the illustrated form.",
